<title>DENMARK: DANISH JUNE UNEMPLOYMENT FALLS TO 8.0 PCT.</title>
<headline>DANISH JUNE UNEMPLOYMENT FALLS TO 8.0 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.0 percent of the workforce in June 1997, down from 8.1 percent in May, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				 June 1997	May 1997    June 1996</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate     8.0 pct	  8.1 pct     8.8 pct*</p>
<p>    Total unemployed	221,600	  224,200*    243,800*</p>
<p>	    *Revised</p>
<p>All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast seasonally adjusted June year-on-year unemployment of 8.0 percent.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652.</p>
</text>
